      "f0000001-0000-7000-8000-000000000001": {
        "tag": "rich-text",
        "id": "f0000001-0000-7000-8000-000000000001",
        "content": "# The Gromov Collapse\n\nThe punchline of the entire framework. The ncreel's virtual cylinder S^1 with tree-structured tablet contents creates a warped product M = S^1 x_f T. At large scales, M is quasi-isometric to T (the tree factor) because S^1 is compact.\n\nTherefore:\n- Gromov boundary of M = Gromov boundary of T\n- Cheeger constant of M ~ Cheeger constant of T > 0\n- Mixing time ~ O(log |M|)\n- The cylinder doesn't matter\n\n## The Chain\n```\nNegative curvature (delta-hyperbolic)\n  => Exponential volume growth\n  => Positive Cheeger constant h(G) > 0\n  => Cheeger inequality: gap >= h^2/(2d)\n  => Spectral gap: 1 - lambda_2 >= const > 0\n  => Mixing time: O(log n)\n```\n\nThis is what Gromov would say: everything reduces to the hyperbolicity of the content trees. The presentation layer (reel, cylinder, UI) is a bounded geometric nuisance."
      },
